// AC#4 NEGATIVE fixture (TASK-0048.04) — `on_violation = count` must be
// REJECTED on tier-3 (no Drop-guard summary sink on bare metal).
//
// Identical placement to naive.sched.nuc plus a `check loop i :
// on_violation = count` directive. The tier-1 count action prints its
// summary at a Drop-guard's `main`-return Drop; a bare-metal firmware
// spins forever in `loop {}` so that Drop never fires
// (docs/check-loop-latency-max.md §3). The embedded backend rejects this
// with a typed EmitError forward-linking the tier-3 count-sink follow-up
// (TASK-0048.08) and directing the user to on_violation=log. This schedule
// is used ONLY by the check_loop_count_is_rejected_with_followup_link unit
// test; it does NOT produce a runnable firmware (it is meant to be
// rejected).

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host };

    place load_input    on host;
    place load_input_b  on host;
    place save_output   on host;
    place add           on host;

    check loop i : latency_max = 1ns, on_violation = count;
}
